Knowing that  $-2 \le \sin(x)+\sin(y)\le 2$  for all  $x,y \in \mathbb{R}$ , we expand (i) to: $-2 \le -2-f(x+y) < \sin(x)+\sin(y) < 2-f(x+y) \le 2$  (ii);

